<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "cache-mover">
<!ENTITY author    "alanstrok">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.04.11d">
<!ENTITY launch    "Settings/cache-mover">
<!ENTITY gitURL    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alanstrok/unraid-cache-mover/claude/tv-show-episode-moving-G9EMM">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "&gitURL;/cache-mover-dev.plg">
<!ENTITY plgPATH   "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY plgNAME   "&name;-&version;-x86_64">
<!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY packages  "/boot/config/plugins/&name;/packages">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        launch="&launch;"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        min="6.12.13"
        support="https://github.com/alanstrok/unraid-cache-mover">

<CHANGES>
 ###2026.04.11d (plex-dev branch)
  - fix: on-deck age filter now also applies to the progression branch
  - stale on-deck shows (older than TV On Deck Max Age) no longer trigger pre-caching

 ###2026.04.11c (plex-dev branch)
  - add move mode (precache_move=yes): files are MOVED not copied, only one copy at a time
  - pre-cache: rsync --remove-source-files from array to SSD
  - evict: rsync --remove-source-files from SSD back to array via /mnt/$target_keephours
  - applies to both TV episodes and movies
  - new UI field: Move Mode (yes/no) in the Plex Pre-Cache section

 ###2026.04.11b (plex-dev branch)
  - fix memory: replace ls -l /proc/*/fd/* glob with fuser (constant memory vs hundreds of MB)
  - fix leaking logger subshells: named FIFO with deterministic cleanup on exit/signal
  - pre-populate mover-tuning ignore list BEFORE first rsync to avoid races with Unraid Mover
  - add --partial to rsync so interrupted transfers resume
  - log when cache_mover_plex receives SIGINT / SIGTERM / SIGHUP

 ###2026.04.11 (plex-dev branch)
  - TV / Movie split: separate subfolder + on-deck-age settings per media type
  - fix progression mode: cache "next one + X" (was X) when nothing is playing
  - UI: Plex Pre-Cache section split into TV Shows and Movies sub-sections
  - relabel "Next Episodes to Pre-Cache" -> "Extra Episodes to Pre-Cache" (behavior unchanged)
  - watched-eviction blast radius now scoped to tv_subfolders regex

 ###2026.04.10 (plex-dev branch)
  - Plex-aware per-episode pre-caching (precache_enabled=yes)
  - caches currently-playing episode + next N unwatched (walks across season boundaries)
  - pre-caches On Deck items within a configurable recency window (TV + movies)
  - evicts watched episodes on the next run, including matching sidecars
  - preserves folder structure for Unraid /mnt/user fuse merge
  - new UI section: Next Episodes, On Deck Max Age, Include Movies, Specials, Kodi-sidecars
  - Jellyfin/Emby and legacy Plex behaviour are unchanged (gated by precache_enabled)
</CHANGES>

<!--
  Dev / test build that installs directly from the alanstrok fork on the
  claude/tv-show-episode-moving-G9EMM branch. Paths (/boot/config/plugins/cache-mover,
  /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/cache-mover) are identical to the upstream plugin, so this
  installs on top of (or in place of) the official cache-mover. Uninstalling and
  reinstalling the upstream .plg reverts cleanly.
-->

<FILE Name="&emhttp;/README.md">
 <INLINE>
  **Cache Mover (dev build: Plex per-episode pre-cache)**

  Plex-aware build of cache-mover. Caches only the currently-playing episode plus the next
  N unwatched episodes, pre-caches recent On Deck items, and evicts watched episodes on the
  next run to keep the cache footprint minimal while keeping it hot.

  Enable in Settings -> CACHE-MOVER -> "Plex Pre-Cache Enabled: yes".
 </INLINE>
</FILE>

